  "why": "The whole-body model applies each US pin load at the stay node (force + the lane moment, h1_lanes.lane_items): the arm carries no pin load there, so its root sees only the stay's global stress. The stub model routes the pin load through the cheeks and the arm into the root, which is what loads that root; its fixed stub ends leave out the lower branch (conservative) and the global stay stress (unconservative). The stub number is the one to design to until the T1 / MT-1 strain gauge at the US1 root settles it."
